### Example 5 — Parallel named items, each with a line → card_grid (NOT a bullet or icon list)

**Input brief:**
Headline: Teams open the tool at five moments in the working day
Narrative role: Show when usage happens, so the launch plan targets those moments.
Key messages:
1. Stand-up (09:00-09:30): the board is reviewed live with the whole team
2. Deep work (10:00-12:00): tasks are updated quietly, one person at a time
3. Hand-off (14:00-15:00): work passes between time zones
4. Review (16:00-17:00): managers approve the day's changes
5. Late fixes (after 20:00): urgent edits from mobile — the fastest-growing moment
Visual emphasis: late fixes is the moment to win

**Correct output:**
```json
{
  "slide_type": "content",
  "components": [
    {
      "component_id": "slide_title",
      "kind": "title",
      "weight": "minor",
      "{{ content_field }}": {"title": "Teams open the tool at five moments in the working day"}
    },
    {
      "component_id": "usage_moments",
      "kind": "card_grid",
      "items": 5,
      "weight": "hero",
      "design_hint": "inverted panel on the Late fixes card; clock icon in each card",
      "{{ content_field }}": {
        "card_layout": "grid",
        "cards": [
          {"title": "Stand-up", "tag": "09:00-09:30", "body": "The board is reviewed live with the whole team"},
          {"title": "Deep work", "tag": "10:00-12:00", "body": "Tasks are updated quietly, one person at a time"},
          {"title": "Hand-off", "tag": "14:00-15:00", "body": "Work passes between time zones"},
          {"title": "Review", "tag": "16:00-17:00", "body": "Managers approve the day's changes"},
          {"title": "Late fixes", "tag": "After 20:00", "body": "Urgent edits from mobile — the fastest-growing moment", "tone": "good", "key_phrase": "fastest-growing moment"}
        ],
        "focus_card": 4
      }
    }
  ],
  "layout_hint": "usage_moments fills the slide as two rows of cards (3 + 2); Late fixes is the one dark card"
}
```

**Why card_grid and not a bullet list:** the five moments ARE the slide — each is a named item with its own time and detail. A card per moment gives each one room, keeps its detail beside it, and fills the slide; an icon list would leave the card half empty and drop the detail. Use bullet_list only for plain takeaways or actions.

